This is a known breaking change. Android deprecated `SOFT_INPUT_ADJUST_RESIZE` (API 30+), so `WindowSoftInputModeAdjust.Resize` no longer resizes the layout in .NET 10 MAUI.

### Recommended fix: handle IME (keyboard) insets manually

In **`Platforms/Android/MainActivity.cs`**, apply a window-insets listener that adds bottom padding when the keyboard appears:

```csharp
using Android.Views;
using AndroidX.Core.View;
using Microsoft.Maui.Platform;

public class MainActivity : MauiAppCompatActivity
{
    protected override void OnCreate(Bundle? savedInstanceState)
    {
        base.OnCreate(savedInstanceState);

        // Listen for keyboard (IME) inset changes
        if (Window?.DecorView is View decorView)
        {
            ViewCompat.SetOnApplyWindowInsetsListener(decorView, new KeyboardInsetsListener());
        }
    }

    private class KeyboardInsetsListener : Java.Lang.Object, IOnApplyWindowInsetsListener
    {
        public WindowInsetsCompat OnApplyWindowInsets(View view, WindowInsetsCompat insets)
        {
            var imeInsets = insets.GetInsets(WindowInsetsCompat.Type.Ime());
            var systemBarInsets = insets.GetInsets(WindowInsetsCompat.Type.SystemBars());

            // Use the larger of IME or system bar bottom inset
            int bottomPadding = Math.Max(imeInsets.Bottom, systemBarInsets.Bottom);
            view.SetPadding(view.PaddingLeft, view.PaddingTop, view.PaddingRight, bottomPadding);

            return insets;
        }
    }
}
```

### Why this works

- `WindowInsetsCompat.Type.Ime()` gives you the keyboard height in pixels.
- When the keyboard opens, the decor view's bottom padding grows, pushing your input bar up.
- When it closes, padding returns to the system bar size.

### Tips for your chat layout

- Use a `Grid` with the `Entry`/`Editor` in the last row (`Auto` height) and your message list in a `*` row above it.
- You can remove any old `WindowSoftInputModeAdjust` calls — they're no longer needed.
- MAUI's built-in `KeyboardAutoManagerScroll` scrolls to focused fields but **doesn't resize the layout**, so the insets approach above is the right one for chat UIs.
